  "body": "When a readable byte stream is closed while the first pending pull-into descriptor holds only part of an element, `ReadableByteStreamControllerClose` used to error the stream and throw. This isn't great for two reasons:\n* Both \"close a ReadableStream\" and `ReadableByteStreamTee` use `!`, so `ReadableByteStreamControllerClose` wasn't even *allowed* to throw.\n* Fundamentally, this is not a valid reason to error the stream: it's not the fault of the underlying byte source that the BYOB reader is trying to do a multi-byte read when the source is out of bytes and wants to close the stream.\n \nInstead, the stream now becomes close-requested. When the underlying byte source responds to the pending BYOB request, the incomplete element is put back into the queue, and the pending read-into requests are handled as if they were made after `close()`: each one is fulfilled with as many whole elements as are available, or fails with a `TypeError` if not even one element is available. The stream becomes closed once the queue is drained. Similarly, a `read(view)` on a close-requested stream whose queue cannot reach the minimum fill no longer errors the stream.\n \nFixes #1387. Alternative to #1388.\n\n- [ ] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\n   * …\n   * …\n- [x] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\n   * https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/64155\n- [ ] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\n   * Chromium: …\n   * Gecko: …\n   * WebKit: …\n   * Deno: …\n   * Node.js: …\n- [ ] [MDN issue](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) is filed: …\n- [x] The top of this comment includes a [clear commit message](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/COMMITTING.md) to use. <!-- If you created this PR from a single commit, Github copied its message. Otherwise, you need to add a commit message yourself. -->\n\n(See [WHATWG Working Mode: Changes](https://whatwg.org/working-mode#changes) for more details.)\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/streams/1389.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 15, 2026, 10:15 AM UTC (d5ed853)\">Preview</a> | <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/streams/1389/b9ba9f4...d5ed853.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 15, 2026, 10:15 AM UTC (d5ed853)\">Diff</a>",
